+
+Assistant recording uses audio actually consumed by the local Discord player,
+separately from conversational input, so unheard generated text is not recorded
+as speech or fed back to the bot. Finalization joins accepted playback and speech
+before closing the source. Notes are marked partial when the source reported lost
+audio/transcription or the stored summary read omitted earlier utterances.
+Bounded model inputs cover consecutive portions and reduce their ordered notes;
+a partial transcript cannot establish that the whole meeting had no substance.
+
+## Capture lifecycle ownership
+
+OpenClaw's internal `startConfiguredTranscriptCapture` helper serves a native
+service that already owns a configured recording lifecycle. It accepts `config`,
+the exact provider `source`, startup `abortSignal`, and `logger`, with optional
+`stateDir` and `title`. Its handle exposes the admitted `session` and a coalesced,
+retryable `finish({ stoppedAt?, onCaptureStopped? })` operation. The callback
+confirms that the exact source was released; the returned promise also joins
+native append drainage, guarded summary persistence, and provider cleanup.
+A retained handle cannot stop a replacement capture. Capture owners load lazily
+and share the existing database and scheduler.
+
+Providers deliver final accepted utterances before terminal status and mark
+`TranscriptSourceStatus.coverage: "partial"` when that subscription lost audio or
+transcription. Core persists coverage and retains the summary input/revision
+compare-and-swap guards. A closed provider connection alone cannot establish
+finalization.
